   2632  f980							; --- Cell walk (cell_collision_plan 2.1): test the PF buffers directly ---
   2633  f980							; The ZP rect cache ($CC-$DF, 5-slot limit) is gone from THIS walker: the
   2634  f980							; render buffers PF0/1/2Buf ARE the map (BombMarkWalls punches bomb holes
   2635  f980							; into them), so room complexity is unbounded and geometry parity is proven
   2636  f980							; by tools/test_cell_map.py (box vs geometry, all models/rooms).
   2637  f980							; Prologue ranges (all left-half space): CollisionCellY = top row,
   2638  f980							; CollisionEndY = bottom row, CollisionEndX = min col, CollisionCellX = max
   2639  f980							; col — cols are endpoint-mirrored above, so ALWAYS 0-19 here (no in-loop
   2640  f980							; mirror; bank2 display-space walkers add their own when they convert).
   2641  f980							; RectCount = running row, CollisionX = running col (both were walk temps
   2642  f980							; before — same ZP, no new allocation).
