   2842  fb37							; jsr-entered from the kernel row-advance (rts back, then `jmp .Line` —
   2843  fb37							; DASM has no external-local syntax so the loop re-entry stays in-scope)
   2844  fb37							; while RowIdx == VcrBand and VcrNext in 1..4. Replaces the .Row setup
   2845  fb37							; line for slices 1-4 (slice0 ran via the kernel-entry .Row with the
   2846  fb37							; derived 8-line count):
   2847  fb37							;   ranges   [0,9) [9,18) [18,31) [31,40) [40,49)  = 5 setups + 44 bodies
   2848  fb37							;	      = 49 WSYNCs — exactly band0's original count (wall unchanged).
   2849  fb37							; ENABL/ENAM1 = per-slice state gates (ball $ff/$00, left-mirror M1
   2850  fb37							; $02/$00 — Step 4) — written early on the setup line (well before the
   2851  fb37							; block's ball pixels, so no transition seam); PF/palette persist from
   2852  fb37							; .Row's band setup. Setup line WSYNCS (visible) but does NOT enter .Line —
   2853  fb37							; Y (running A0) must still advance so the next .Line pass indexes the
   2854  fb37							; correct sprite row (bug: skipped iny delayed GRP0 3 lines when armed).
   2855  fb37							; .Line inherits Y = A0+1 exactly as after a body WSYNC.
   2856  fb37							; Cycles: tail ≈19 + body ≈36 + jsr/rts 12 ≈ 67-71 from the previous
   2857  fb37							; WSYNC (<= 76 → the setup line does not stall; band0 keeps its measured
   2858  fb37							; wall contribution). Step 4: +6/+8 for the ENAM1 pair, −5 from moving
   2859  fb37							; `inc VcrNext` after the WSYNC — net inside the same window.
   2860  fb37							; SBmask entries = VcrState bit per slice; SBod = bodies per slice
   2861  fb37							; (index 0 = slice0, correct-but-unused: slice0 count comes from the
   2862  fb37							; kernel-entry .Row derive).
